ore_fcf_yield":null,"_gate_int_coverage":null,"_gp_int_coverage":null,"_score_int_coverage":null,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gate_accruals":0.003962891020146111,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":22.2,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.11187655627199604,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":82.3,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.0019605429777072025,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":97.5,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.0429500899877191,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":22.8,"_gate_rev_durability":0.12316930063818843,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":86.6,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03734061536709033,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":52.6,"_gate_share_shrink":0.062004986060128386,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.013465990709705446,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":77.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.01023,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":6.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Valley National Bancorp operates as the holding company for Valley National Bank that provides various commercial, private banking, retail, insurance, and wealth management financial services products. The company operates through Consumer Banking, Commercial Banking, and Treasury and Corporate other segments. It offers non-interest bearing, savings, NOW, money market, and time deposit accounts; commercial and industrial, commercial real estate, construction, residential mortgage, and automobile loans; loans secured by the cash surrender value of life insurance; home equity loans and lines of credit; automobile financing; and secured and unsecured other consumer loans. The company also invests in various securities and interest-bearing deposits with other banks; and provides international banking services. In addition, it offers investment services for individuals and small to medium sized businesses; and trusts investment strategies designed for various investment profiles and objectives. Further, the company provides trust services, such as living and testamentary trusts, investment management, custodial and escrow services, and estate administration to individuals; tax credit advisory services; brokerage services; property and casualty, life, health, and title insurance agency services; and health care equipment lending and other commercial equipment leasing services, as well as private banking and management services. Additionally, it offers niche financial services, including loan and deposit products for homeowners associations, cannabis-related business banking, and venture banking; online, mobile, and telephone banking services; credit cards; and automated teller machine services. Valley National Bancorp was founded in 1927 and is headquartered in Morristown, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ira D. Robbins CPA | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 50 | Compensation: $3.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $551K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $89K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Valley National Bancorp is a mid-cap financial services business with a $7.9B market cap on $2.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $326M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 16 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.57\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["35 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Valley National Bancorp (NASDAQ:VLY) Cut to \u201cMarket Perform\u201d at Keefe, Bruyette & Woods","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/valley-national-bancorp-nasdaqvly-cut-to-market-perform-at-keefe-bruyette-woods.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794471904.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.7,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Valley National Bancorp (VLY) Wins Key Regulatory Clearance For Providence Acquisition","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-vly/valley-national-bancorp/news/valley-national-bancorp-vly-wins-key-regulatory-clearance-fo","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794381964.833,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.929,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["regulatory"]},{"title":"Valley National Bancorp (VLY) Could Be 14% Undervalued After Its Core Deposit Growth Story","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-vly/valley-national-bancorp/news/valley-national-bancorp-vly-could-be-14-undervalued-after-it","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794291750.571,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.898,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Here's W